  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_turmeric_cb15d9b17e39305a04153a0938c91176706db792216569192186daf1a2aa02936bc">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>meaning unknown in earliest occurrences (measured in dozens); turmeric, the aromatic and pungent root-stock of the East Indian plant (Curcuma longa), or the powder made of this, the chief ingredient in curry powder, used also in dyeing yellow, and as a chemical test, and in the East as a condiment and medicinally; also applied by English herbalists to the root of Tormentil, and to the root-stock of Sanguinaria canadensis (OED s.v. turmeric n. 1)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
